---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTABlock from '../../components/CTABlock.astro';
import { ROUTES } from '../../i18n/routes';
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  active="story"
  title="Our Story — Casa Lana"
  description="From yearly holidays to a place of our own in Spain: the story behind Casa Lana in Hondón de las Nieves."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Story</span>
      <h1>From yearly holidays to a place of our own in Spain</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap story">
      <p>
        In 1996, Evelien went to Spain on an Erasmus exchange. She got to know the language
        and the culture there, and fell in love with the country. That love didn't really come
        out of nowhere — since she was three, she had travelled to Spain with her parents
        almost every year. The Spanish bug had bitten early.
      </p>
      <p>
        And apparently that bug is contagious. First Jurgen caught it, and later so did our
        children, Lukas and Helena. Over the years, Spain became a place our family always
        loved returning to.
      </p>
      <p>
        Having a place of our own in Spain had long been a dream. Ideally somewhere between
        Valencia and Alicante. Not on the busy coast, but not completely remote either. We
        were looking for a place where we could find peace, while still having plenty to
        discover whenever we felt like it.
      </p>
      <p>Dreams stay dreams if you do nothing with them.</p>
      <p>
        So we started looking. We had one important condition: everyone in our family had to
        feel good about the house we'd buy.
      </p>
      <p>That didn't exactly make the search easy. Let's just say we were rather picky.</p>
      <p>Until we found this place.</p>
      <p>
        A spacious house, a beautiful pool, 10,000 m² of land, mountains all around us, and
        above all, a lot of peace and quiet. No rows of hotels, no crowded beaches, no mass
        tourism. Just pulling the gate shut behind you and feeling the pace slow down on its
        own.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's exactly what we love here ourselves. Our everyday life is busy enough as it is.
        Here, for a while, nothing has to happen.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to cook at home in the evening and enjoy a meal together? Everything's here. Want
        to go out, find a restaurant, visit a market, explore a city, or head to the coast?
        You just get in the car — there's surprisingly much within reach.
      </p>
      <p>
        We bought Casa Lana first and foremost for ourselves and our family. And we're happy
        to share it with people looking for the same thing we were: peace, space, time for
        each other, and a break from the daily rush.
      </p>
      <p>
        That can be with your family, with friends, or with two couples together. Anyone
        looking to spend a few weeks somewhere quiet, working in between, will find all the
        space they need here too.
      </p>
      <p>
        A wild party weekend doesn't fit with Casa Lana — there are plenty of other places in
        Spain for that. We have a good relationship with the people who live in the area, and
        we respect the peace that exists here.
      </p>
      <p>
        We chose and furnished this place with a great deal of love. And with just as much
        pleasure, we open it up to people who want to enjoy it and take good care of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That way, Casa Lana doesn't stay just our story — it also becomes a place where other
        families and friends can make beautiful memories of their own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABlock
    title="Fancy adding to our story?"
    text="Check availability and book your own little corner of calm in Spain."
    ctaLabel="Check availability"
    ctaHref={ROUTES.availability.en}
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-intro {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .story {
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .story p {
    color: #3a362c;
  }
</style>
